{arialbld}Kurt Rorscham{arial}

Campaign HQ
Mülscheim-on-Zar










The news from Zwalonia is bad.{pause}

Alex Kolman and the 1st Normo Army's plan was to block the Psychos in the north, preventing them from falling on our back as we charged eastwards.{pause}

It worked as planned, Kolman had crushed three Tekton divisions in the north of Fromance before we even took Kolmar.{pause}

Problem is, buoyed by his success and our apparent ease of progress, that old fogey, Alex, preferred grandstanding over waiting to be joined by Spirex and the 2nd Schyzo Army marching up from the south.{pause}

About a week ago, his troops crossed the Valstar so as to enter Zwalonia, hoping for a spectacular tour-de-force at the naval base of {arialbld}Watoo.{arial}{pause} 

Unfortunately Tankred von Tekton was waiting for them. Meanwhile Otton had folded back to {arialbld}Charleroi{arial} with his 2nd armours division, the "Black Boars", cutting off any retreat.{pause}

Now the old man is pinned down at {arialbld}Bastogne{arial} with no reinforcements within 300km.{pause}

The situation stinks. Barring a miracle, the noose will tighten up around Alex's neck and the entire 1st Normo Army's gonna get choked like a chicken.{pause}

The Allied High Strategic Command and I think the same: the only miracle worker we know in the neighbourhood, is YOU {name}!{pause}

There's no time to lose {rank}, you must fly to the salvation of Alex's old knees. And while you're at it, try to get your tanks to fly too.{pause}


I almost forgot: Otton von Tekton asked Alex Kolman to surrender. You know what the old man answered, and I quote: "nuts!".{pause}


{offset150}3rd Schyzo Army

{arialbld}Kurt Rorscham{arial}



